From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] treewide: build only for Linux 6.18 and 7.3

Drop every LINUX_VERSION_CODE branch for kernels older than 6.18 and
fold the per-version compatibility patches into this one.

Linux 7.2 removed the IGMPV3_MRC() and IGMPV3_QQIC() macros. Decode the
IGMPv3 and MLDv2 8-bit exponential fields with the module's own
MLDV2_EXP(), which already decodes the MLDv2 MRC.

Linux 7.2 also typed the bind address as struct sockaddr_unsized. Bind
the nl80211 event socket with kernel_bind() and the size of the
sockaddr_nl it passes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---

